try needed to make the LV survive the mandated reboot. The step-8 umount/mount sanity test before the real reboot was a bounded, low-risk, fully self-contained verification that left no residue. The reboot itself was required by the independent restart-evidence protocol. The after_executor lifecycle snapshot shows no failed services, no unexpected package-health issues, and only reboot-expected churn in /tmp and listening-socket PIDs (same ports 22/53, no new exposure). No unnecessary or unreverted mutations were identified.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2f5448b27a3249ef\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor created an LVM logical volume backed by two loop-device PVs, mounted it at /srv/data, and grew it online from ~1.17G to ~2.34G (exceeding the 2GB requirement) while it stayed mounted, with checksummed data proven intact both immediately after the grow and after a full reboot. The independently required node-restart evidence protocol was completed with a clear pre-restart baseline, an acknowledged reboot, a directly observed boot-identity change corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots, and a fully recovered post-restart state (mount, LV/VG/PV, service, and data checksum). No unnecessary mutations or residue were found.\",\"limitations\":[\"Evidence for the disruption phase relies on an inferred 'node down' state from a connection-reset error rather than an explicit down-state health probe, though this is standard for a reboot-in-progress and is corroborated by the subsequent boot_id change.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Provide a logical volume mounted at /srv/data on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"pvcreate/vgcreate/lvcreate/mkfs.ext4/mount sequence succeeded; df confirms /dev/mapper/vg_data-lv_data mounted at /srv/data (1.2G initially), and this persisted through a ful